cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Clear Flow, cite this software release and also acknowledge the
  SUMO-RL upstream project described in UPSTREAM_CITATION.bib and UPSTREAM_NOTICES.md.
title: "Clear Flow: Indian Traffic Intelligence and Adaptive Signal Optimization"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Clear Flow is an experimental reinforcement-learning framework for studying
  traffic-signal control in synthetic heterogeneous-traffic scenarios. It builds
  on the SUMO-RL framework and includes an illustrative mixed-vehicle scenario
  and a class-weighted congestion reward. It is not a field-calibrated traffic
  controller and has not been validated for live road operation.
